{"title":"2000 AIME I Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9e1e81f3f49967c65f2d0c3f14b7ef1b71d8650.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; v &lt; u$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b9c00a850de1eaf2452caa17bfdd889c1bd518b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (u,v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Reflection\" title=\"Reflection\">reflection</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> across the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40fee4603b4536f856dde720ee499468ace443f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> across the y-axis, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> across the x-axis, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> across the y-axis. The area of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pentagon\" title=\"Pentagon\">pentagon</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/4/194d98563bb5459996531f6ed210703f6ce98a34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$451$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/7/387885f0e6ec1245f344fd1b192210e4a689e7f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u + v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/9/d49b785d1030eea278bb89aaeeef04946478a11e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pointpen = black; pathpen = linewidth(0.7) + black; size(180); pair A=(11,10), B=(10,11), C=(-10, 11), D=(-10, -11), E=(10, -11); D(D(MP(&quot;A\\ (u,v)&quot;,A,(1,0)))--D(MP(&quot;B&quot;,B,N))--D(MP(&quot;C&quot;,C,N))--D(MP(&quot;D&quot;,D))--D(MP(&quot;E&quot;,E))--cycle); D((-15,0)--(15,0),linewidth(0.6),Arrows(5)); D((0,-15)--(0,15),linewidth(0.6),Arrows(5)); D((-15,-15)--(15,15),linewidth(0.6),Arrows(5)); [/asy]\" width=\"302\" height=\"268\" /></center> \n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b9c00a850de1eaf2452caa17bfdd889c1bd518b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (u,v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />, we can find the coordinates of the other points: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d93e4ae5db8c7f402fbd070a556330db77bfa78f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (v,u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60d897c4edee6c13eed0639b1dc7c2ff9d7a2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (-v,u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/10141b03bcb41c1110fdc3371754d86a7c0cf8c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = (-v,-u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/120aef896b771f685cd4d03a035d26f47ff710a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = (v,-u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />. If we graph those points, we notice that since the latter four points are all reflected across the x/y-axis, they form a rectangle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is a triangle. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af420a6e2b903f5295dd8f65f321545f69e44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCDE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/9/7b9842c3fd3a63243da7d2adbca5750e3c8af44a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2u)(2v) = 4uv$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" /> and the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4e49327b0546744e6c59231a441b2d0c3f0e105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(2u)(u-v) = u^2 - uv$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"187\" height=\"37\" />. Adding these together, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4d130c98a52d2d982eb1edc3e7231bddcb1a8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^2 + 3uv = u(u+3v) = 451 = 11 \\cdot 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"293\" height=\"19\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f03710a9ffbf0ecba4ae631d6f3bd28ff7f48f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u,v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> are positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/8/168f11d5c764e103cea325fce9ac566168b262a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u+3v&gt;u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />, and by matching factors we get either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f6ef23265d1cc6c70f495bae2357e013494129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u,v) = (1,150)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/6780fc715ba7fc69be32d9c9ce47071bbabe956c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(11,10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e05e6fbce77d6c70a0d934549e4328bb7cebe82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v &lt; u$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"10\" /> the latter case is the answer, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d8290ca7ef555d14d276d2420d089b14db1855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u+v = \\boxed{021}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"107\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We find the coordinates like in the solution above: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b9c00a850de1eaf2452caa17bfdd889c1bd518b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (u,v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d93e4ae5db8c7f402fbd070a556330db77bfa78f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (v,u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60d897c4edee6c13eed0639b1dc7c2ff9d7a2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (-v,u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/10141b03bcb41c1110fdc3371754d86a7c0cf8c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = (-v,-u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/120aef896b771f685cd4d03a035d26f47ff710a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = (v,-u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />. Then we notice pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> fits into a rectangle of side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6468d73806452f8918729498ce100a0ebfb7f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u+v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/a/e7a33ef8bb14bef8ed164f55c443a0ca441b9abe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\" />, giving us two triangles, each with hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. First, we can solve for the first triangle. Using the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, we discover the side lengths are both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c3621ffd4f1364adeca03182863f4d4b216978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u-v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" />, so the area of the triangle of hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/b/73b00a4e962611ad7362317fe3e74a131e05b114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(u-v)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />. Next, we can solve for the second triangle. Using the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, we discover the side lengths are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c3621ffd4f1364adeca03182863f4d4b216978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u-v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6468d73806452f8918729498ce100a0ebfb7f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u+v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" />, so the area of the triangle of hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a2c0d1a803e226be8545bf7e7e69dc7b832f96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(u-v)(u+v) = \\frac{1}{2}(u^2-v^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"236\" height=\"38\" />. Now, let’s subtract the area of these 2 triangles from the rectangle giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/2562daa55fe8e992450a189ba00cdf92ebc28a3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u+v)(2u)-\\frac{1}{2}(u-v)^2-\\frac{1}{2}(u^2-v^2)=451 —&gt; u^2+3uv=451 -&gt; u(u+3v)=451$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"664\" height=\"38\" />. Next, we take note of the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e1f2a6996a7ab917b003b0e585974fbb65fb8fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u+3v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> are both factors of 451, and since both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e1f2a6996a7ab917b003b0e585974fbb65fb8fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u+3v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, thus giving us two cases, where either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cab673758c144b93863e2c17470aa3ee77e95d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/01141543b65a0a05def01d4852b586ef229f2d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. After trying both, the only working pair of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d7cc0aaa3c34fd4a50a506fb22de40dfff3ed09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u,v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> where both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are integers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/01141543b65a0a05def01d4852b586ef229f2d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/e/73e2dd488c5f1f51c0e29c243d99a8d06885bdf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />, thus meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28d21a65b6a1d5aef535589aa1d52825b1f526b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u + v =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf7653858ab99f5fdb38bc4c692780c5d12519b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{021}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~Aeioujyot\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We find the coordinates like in the solution above: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b9c00a850de1eaf2452caa17bfdd889c1bd518b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (u,v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d93e4ae5db8c7f402fbd070a556330db77bfa78f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (v,u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60d897c4edee6c13eed0639b1dc7c2ff9d7a2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (-v,u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/10141b03bcb41c1110fdc3371754d86a7c0cf8c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = (-v,-u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/120aef896b771f685cd4d03a035d26f47ff710a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = (v,-u)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />. Then we apply the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Shoelace_Theorem\" title=\"Shoelace Theorem\">Shoelace Theorem</a>. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c15f2f6d53bc93d6a5feec8e644330f3275959e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A =  \\frac{1}{2}[(u^2 + vu + vu + vu + v^2) - (v^2 - uv - uv - uv -u^2)] = 451\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c6fca8c04af8ce8951f1d69ae70cfec40861d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}(2u^2 + 6uv) = 451\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f909e0f6d466056264cff3f4376f0bc65829de1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[u(u + 3v) = 451\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb52634ff5bb73e1eaf8eb3480eae36e8d30232f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u,v) = (11, 10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a95635fa095c7d39973879a689df665a21ec48ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,150)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />, but since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e05e6fbce77d6c70a0d934549e4328bb7cebe82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v &lt; u$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"10\" />, then the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf7653858ab99f5fdb38bc4c692780c5d12519b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{021}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a hre